no pairs him against ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"ac087719-147c-47fa-9bb0-801f7a039ca7","displayText":"El Cieguito de Nagua","occurrenceId":"f3bce1fc-210d-4ce0-97f7-bc89fb9cff6e"}},{"text":" across a single record — the head-to-head format típico has long used to put two accordionists in the same room. The man he had drummed behind two decades earlier was now on the other side of the billing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"A lo Moderno","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The tag is his own and he uses it everywhere: on the records, in the song titles, as the name of his page. He works out of Miami now, and he has not stopped — El Palo Prendío came out in 2026, close to forty years after he first stood in front of his own conjunto. He and Fidelina still play together.","type":"text"}]}]}'::jsonb FOR UPDATE) THEN
