**Legado**

Aguakate está documentado a través de sus álbumes con «Universal Latino» y de la carrera posterior de Correa, que continúa con el nombre Shino Aguakate.' WHERE id = '85598d90-481f-404e-9f87-24b099ed43ec'::uuid;
  PERFORM id FROM public.upsert_editorial_document('artist_biography', '85598d90-481f-404e-9f87-24b099ed43ec'::uuid, 'en', 1, 'published', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Aguakate is a Dominican merengue típico group formed in New York in 2003 around the singer Gerpis Correa, known as ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","displayText":"Shino Aguakate","occurrenceId":"293a06a4-2f8b-43b9-b6eb-82dc04593ba8"}},{"text":", which mixed the accordion sound with reggaeton and urban merengue.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Formation","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Music directories say the group was created by José Mateo Peligro together with Correa, on the label «Peligro Records». The name comes from a word Correa used constantly to say that everything was fine; the producer took it as a proposal for the band. The early lineup listed accordionist Belarminio Liriano, Pedro Lantigua on congas, Waldi on guitar, Alejandro on bass, DJ Chucky on piano, Diógenes on saxophone, Fermín Flores on backing vocals and Eddie on percussion.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Records","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In 2004 the group signed with «Universal Latino» and released its debut «De otra galaxia», a twelve-track album that includes «La gallinita», «Mueva esa vaina», «La agarradera», «El divorcio», «Solo con un beso» and «Reggaeton ripiao». In March 2004 came the live album «En vivo desde Santo Domingo», and the same year «Aguakate vs Krisspy: mano a mano», with "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"15c08a48-b94b-41c8-99d8-53144397c787","displayText":"Krisspy","occurrenceId":"e514e769-7e8d-4fd0-9ac6-653d543d0893"}},{"type":"text","text":", on «Mambo Records». «Crazyssimo» followed in August 2006 with «Tu pussycat» and «La conquista», recorded with "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"059a9e99-5d11-433e-97b9-9c35e57908f1","displayText":"Sergio Vargas","occurrenceId":"51f3dadd-6692-4896-93b1-9a39083e35bb"}},{"type":"text","text":", and «Quiero verte», with "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"6321da6c-e2d5-490a-a4e8-416bbee81edf","displayText":"Don Miguelo","occurrenceId":"f8990271-329e-4a62-8896-fc602533b245"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Split and return","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The group broke up in 2006 when Correa began a solo project as "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"d0941c37-0695-456c-a893-fde9973a4243","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":" with the producer Frasier Hernández, who encouraged him to combine styles. It returned in 2010 with Correa as leader and shareholder, most of the former musicians back and management by «M&M Enterprises». It has toured Jamaica, the Dominican Republic, Puerto Rico, Alaska, Canada and several US cities, and in June 2011 played the «Puerto Rican Festival» organized by the station «La Mega 97.9» at 112th Street and Third Avenue in Manhattan, with «El amor que perdimos», «Danza kuduro» and «Aléjate de mí». In 2015 "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"25c417fc-ccb7-49b3-a5a8-bfbdbcaacd91","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":" appeared with "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"5602ba48-f2d7-4f38-b2a9-fea2aef24aca","occurrenceId":"3b012c7e-a3a8-4116-9b4a-efef5b62323e","displayText":"Oro Sólido"}},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"74b60ddd-3a3d-4983-8ff7-6fdf5f0513ed","occurrenceId":"a8d66a0f-6c46-488f-87bc-afb7b952738b","displayText":"Mala Fe"}},{"type":"text","text":" on «Pussy Cat»."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Style","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"The band played fast merengue típico with rapid instrumental solos and mixed it with romantic merengue, reggaeton and urban rhythms. In «Reggaeton ripiao» the rhythm changes from merengue to a reggaeton pattern adapted for the tambora, a mixture that was controversial among típico purists.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Legacy","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Aguakate is documented through its albums with «Universal Latino» and the later career of Correa, who continues under the name "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"1e794319-7f0d-46fc-bfb9-2ab210078691","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}'::jsonb, 2);
  PERFORM id FROM public.upsert_editorial_document('artist_biography', '85598d90-481f-404e-9f87-24b099ed43ec'::uuid, 'es', 1, 'published', '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Aguakate es un grupo dominicano de merengue típico formado en Nueva York en 2003 en torno al cantante Gerpis Correa, conocido como ","type":"text"},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","displayText":"Shino Aguakate","occurrenceId":"7ca08f0a-9f50-44ca-86c6-d167385c131b"}},{"text":", que mezcló el sonido del acordeón con el reguetón y el merengue urbano.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Formación","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Los directorios musicales dicen que el grupo fue creado por José Mateo Peligro junto con Correa, bajo el sello «Peligro Records». El nombre viene de una palabra que Correa usaba constantemente para decir que todo estaba bien; el productor la tomó como una propuesta para la banda. La alineación inicial incluía al acordeonista Belarminio Liriano, Pedro Lantigua en las congas, Waldi en la guitarra, Alejandro en el bajo, DJ Chucky en el piano, Diógenes en el saxofón, Fermín Flores en los coros y Eddie en la percusión.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Discos","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"En 2004 el grupo firmó con «Universal Latino» y publicó su debut «De otra galaxia», un álbum de doce pistas que incluye «La gallinita», «Mueva esa vaina», «La agarradera», «El divorcio», «Solo con un beso» y «Reggaeton ripiao». En marzo de 2004 salió el álbum en vivo «En vivo desde Santo Domingo», y ese mismo año «Aguakate vs Krisspy: mano a mano», con "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"15c08a48-b94b-41c8-99d8-53144397c787","displayText":"Krisspy","occurrenceId":"eb36aa35-ab39-45bc-8d66-37a47c469f39"}},{"type":"text","text":", en «Mambo Records». «Crazyssimo» siguió en agosto de 2006 con «Tu pussycat» y «La conquista», grabada con "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"059a9e99-5d11-433e-97b9-9c35e57908f1","displayText":"Sergio Vargas","occurrenceId":"307c18ea-2734-4bc1-b3df-82c0dfb8f28d"}},{"type":"text","text":", y «Quiero verte», con "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"6321da6c-e2d5-490a-a4e8-416bbee81edf","displayText":"Don Miguelo","occurrenceId":"a05258bd-90be-4298-b99a-c232ca45d3da"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Separación y regreso","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"El grupo se separó en 2006 cuando Correa empezó un proyecto solista como "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"c571c26a-54b0-4f0f-a52b-5c271fb28bfe","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":" con el productor Frasier Hernández, que lo animó a combinar estilos. Volvió en 2010 con Correa como líder y accionista, la mayoría de los antiguos músicos de regreso y la gestión de «M&M Enterprises». Ha girado por Jamaica, República Dominicana, Puerto Rico, Alaska, Canadá y varias ciudades de Estados Unidos, y en junio de 2011 tocó en el «Festival Puertorriqueño» organizado por la emisora «La Mega 97.9» en la calle 112 con la Tercera Avenida de Manhattan, con «El amor que perdimos», «Danza kuduro» y «Aléjate de mí». En 2015 "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"9dd1eac1-33fb-4a1e-98cd-69e608050e3d","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":" participó con "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"5602ba48-f2d7-4f38-b2a9-fea2aef24aca","occurrenceId":"2fb79a4d-c24c-47c9-83f4-695cd4891ce2","displayText":"Oro Sólido"}},{"type":"text","text":" y "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"74b60ddd-3a3d-4983-8ff7-6fdf5f0513ed","occurrenceId":"236a182e-24a0-45a9-9919-d23ce9d6dc5c","displayText":"Mala Fe"}},{"type":"text","text":" en «Pussy Cat»."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Estilo","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"La banda tocaba merengue típico rápido, con solos instrumentales veloces, y lo mezclaba con merengue romántico, reguetón y ritmos urbanos. En «Reggaeton ripiao» el ritmo pasa del merengue a un patrón de reguetón adaptado a la tambora, una mezcla que resultó polémica entre los puristas del típico.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"text":"Legado","type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Aguakate está documentado a través de sus álbumes con «Universal Latino» y de la carrera posterior de Correa, que continúa con el nombre "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"artistId":"b0dbcca8-3aba-4ace-ae71-c56e3dbd5378","occurrenceId":"5af251a6-4dce-45bb-8f11-f07623c0d839","displayText":"Shino Aguakate"}},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}'::jsonb, 1);
END $editorial_pass$;
SELECT a.slug, a.status, (SELECT jsonb_agg(jsonb_build_object('locale', d.locale, 'revision', d.revision, 'status', d.status) ORDER BY d.locale) FROM public.editorial_documents d WHERE d.owner_artist_id = a.id AND d.document_type = 'artist_biography') AS documents, (SELECT count(*) FROM public.editorial_entity_references r JOIN public.editorial_documents d ON d.id = r.editorial_document_id WHERE d.owner_artist_id = a.id AND d.document_type = 'artist_biography') AS reference_count FROM public.artists a WHERE a.id = '85598d90-481f-404e-9f87-24b099ed43ec'::uuid;
